			"singular": "Water Elemental",
			"plural": "Water Elementals"
		},
		"description": "Water Elementals can be born anywhere the power of Shalassa, the Dragon of Water, reaches: oceans, rivers, lakes or glaciers. The water magic flowing through the ley lines can also give rise to them. Their appearance varies widely with the region and the local water. Their bodies may be made of clear water, sea foam, mist and fog, snowflakes or sheets of ice. When born in deltas and marshes, they may even be made of mud and sewage. Their moods are just as changeable. The Nagas see them as expressions of Shalassa's silent joy, while sailors fear them, for they sometimes drag people off decks or docks and drown them. Larger Water Elementals are often blamed for the sinking of ships.",
