	"h6NeutralLightElemental": {
		"name": {
			"singular": "Light Elemental",
			"plural": "Light Elementals"
		},
		"description": "Light Elementals usually appear at dawn. When dim, reddish rays are refracted by clouds and dew and woven into a visible shape, a Light Elemental is born. These beautiful spirits seem friendly and a little frivolous, and they often help lost travelers. They are wilder than the holy spirits summoned by the followers of Elrath, the Dragon of Light. Although they share the same essence, Light Elementals care nothing for loyalty; they judge by their own standards whether the heart of everyone they meet is pure. When angered, a Light Elemental can burst into a dazzling flash that blinds its enemies. Because of their love for Elrath, the priests of the Holy Empire share a natural affinity with Light Elementals. Among the priesthood there is an order of women knights known as the \"Lightweavers\", whose task is to seek out newborn Light Elementals. They weave the Light Elementals into holy cloth, used to make the garments worn by the Empire's heroes, or bind them into the stained glass that adorns the cathedrals.",
