	"h6NeutralSpectralDragon": {
		"name": {
			"singular": "Phantom Dragon",
			"plural": "Phantom Dragons"
		},
		"description": "Usually, when a dragon senses its death approaching, it flies to the moon, where Asha dwells, to shed its mortal body and be reborn. Yet in very rare cases, a great and violent event at the moment of a dragon's death severs its spiritual essence from its physical form. Its body and soul then become prisoners of the world of Ashan: the former becomes a Bone Dragon, the latter a Phantom Dragon. Different manners and places of death give rise to different Phantom Dragons. Phantom Dragons are driven by an overwhelming need to devour other souls to sustain their form, which also affects their memories. Most Phantom Dragons have gone mad and cannot be controlled; only a few have been subdued by the Lords of Death. Under the guidance of their Archon Belketh, the necromancers have mastered ways to find, capture and bind these mighty undead dragons to serve their goals.",
